{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771181176371,"sessionID":"ses_39d61732dffeDSmzfjmxT906s1","part":{"id":"prt_c629ed5c7001aE4WQ2T8gp1Np5","sessionID":"ses_39d61732dffeDSmzfjmxT906s1","messageID":"msg_c629e8d8c001d436NwO9YXsLEy","type":"tool","callID":"call_458547ad826b4f9f877f37ce","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore test files and testing setup","prompt":"Explore the test files and testing configuration:\n- Find all test files\n- Understand the testing framework being used\n- Identify what tests exist\n- Note test patterns and conventions used\n\nUse \"medium\" level exploration. Return a summary of test coverage and testing setup."},"output":"task_id: ses_39d612a2bffethBbcTb035GUDF (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Test Coverage and Testing Setup Summary\n\n### Testing Framework\n\n**Primary Framework:** Vitest v4.0.18\n- Modern, fast test framework with native TypeScript support\n- Configured in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/vite.config.ts`\n- Environment: jsdom (for DOM-based tests)\n- Global test functions enabled (`describe`, `it`, `expect`)\n\n**Testing Libraries:**\n- `@testing-library/react` v16.3.2 - React component testing\n- `@testing-library/jest-dom` v6.9.1 - Custom DOM matchers\n- `@testing-library/user-event` v14.6.1 - User interaction simulation\n\n**Test Setup:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/test/setup.ts`\n- Imports jest-dom custom matchers\n- Mocks `localStorage` for both `window` and `globalThis` objects\n\n---\n\n### Test Files Found (15 total)\n\n#### Component Tests (7 files):\n1. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/App.test.tsx` - Main App rendering\n2. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.test.tsx` - HUD controls and display\n3. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/ScoreDisplay.test.tsx` - Score formatting and animations\n4. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/UIToggleButton.test.tsx` - UI visibility toggle\n5. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/IntroOverlay.test.tsx` - Intro screen with animations\n6. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.test.tsx` - Grid interaction logic\n7. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.test.tsx` - Canvas utilities\n\n#### Library/Utility Tests (9 files):\n1. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/simulation.test.ts` - Conway's Game of Life rules, grid operations\n2. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/flux.test.ts` - Flux resource management system\n3. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/scoring.test.ts` - Score calculation and formatting\n4. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/interaction.test.ts` - Mouse/touch event handling\n5. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/phase.test.ts` - Phase transition logic and state machine\n6. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/state.test.ts` - State management utilities, localStorage helpers\n7. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/logger.test.ts` - Logging system\n8. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/validation.test.ts` - Input validation utilities\n9. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/movement.test.ts` - Pattern detection, cluster tracking, velocity calculation\n\n---\n\n### Test Patterns and Conventions\n\n#### 1. **Test Structure**\n```typescript\ndescribe('ComponentOrFunctionName', () => {\n  it('should [expected behavior]', () => {\n    // Test implementation\n  })\n})\n```\n\n#### 2. **Component Testing Pattern**\n- Use `render()` from testing-library to mount components\n- Define default props as `defaultProps` object\n- Mock callback functions with `vi.fn()`\n- Type assertions: `'PLANNING' as const` for literal types\n- Element queries: `screen.getByText()`, `screen.queryByText()`\n- User interactions: `userEvent.setup()` + `await user.click()`\n- Assertions: `expect().toBeInTheDocument()`, `expect().toBeDisabled()`\n\n#### 3. **Library/Utility Testing Pattern**\n- Direct function imports from source files\n- Test happy paths, edge cases, and error scenarios\n- Verify immutability with `.not.toBe()` comparisons\n- Test boundaries (min/max values, empty arrays, etc.)\n- Mock complex objects (HTMLCanvasElement, touch events)\n\n#### 4. **Mocking Techniques**\n- `vi.fn()` - Mock function creation\n- `vi.spyOn()` - Spy on existing functions\n- `vi.stubGlobal()` - Mock global window properties\n- `vi.useFakeTimers()` / `vi.advanceTimersByTime()` - Animation testing\n\n#### 5. **Assertion Patterns**\n- DOM presence: `.toBeInTheDocument()`\n- Text matching: `.toHaveTextContent()`\n- CSS classes: `.toHaveClass()`, `.not.toHaveClass()`\n- Equality: `.toEqual()`, `.toBe()`\n- Async behavior: await user events\n- Error handling: expect errors gracefully\n\n---\n\n### Test Coverage Areas\n\n**Core Game Logic:**\n- Conway's Game of Life rules (block, glider patterns)\n- Grid operations (create, clear, random fill, cell manipulation)\n- Toroidal boundary handling\n- Neighbor counting with edge wrapping\n\n**Flux System:**\n- Resource management (place/remove cells)\n- Phase-based refund rules\n- Color-coded flux levels\n- Default values and initialization\n\n**Scoring System:**\n- Pattern classification (MOVER, OSCILLATOR, STATIC)\n- Score calculation with multipliers\n- Milestone detection\n- Score formatting (K, M suffixes)\n- MAX_SAFE_INTEGER capping\n\n**Interaction System:**\n- Mouse and touch event conversion\n- Canvas coordinate mapping\n- DPR (Device Pixel Ratio) scaling\n- Boundary validation\n\n**Phase Management:**\n- State machine transitions (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED)\n- Countdown and timer logic\n- Blocker validation\n- Transition permissions\n\n**Movement Detection:**\n- Connected component finding (8-connectivity)\n- Cluster tracking and matching\n- Velocity calculation\n- Pattern classification\n- Centroid history management\n\n**Utilities:**\n- Input validation (coordinates, numbers, rule sets)\n- State management (actions, reducers, async actions)\n- localStorage helpers with error handling\n- Logger with timestamps and context\n\n---\n\n### Available NPM Scripts\n\n```json\n\"test\": \"vitest\"              // Watch mode\n\"test:run\": \"vitest run\"      // Run once\n\"test:ui\": \"vitest --ui\"      // Interactive UI\n\"test:coverage\": \"vitest run --coverage\"  // Coverage report\n```\n\n---\n\n### Key Observations\n\n**Strengths:**\n1. Comprehensive test coverage across both UI and business logic\n2. Well-organized test structure mirroring source code\n3. Consistent naming conventions\n4. Thorough edge case testing\n5. Proper mocking of external dependencies\n6. Tests are behavior-focused, not implementation-focused\n\n**Testing Quality:**\n- Component tests verify user interactions and rendering\n- Library tests verify pure functions and business logic\n- Integration between components is tested through props\n- Error scenarios are explicitly tested\n- Immutability is verified throughout\n\n**Coverage Gaps:** (None identified - the test suite appears comprehensive for the codebase)\n</task_result>","title":"Explore test files and testing setup","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d612a2bffethBbcTb035GUDF","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771181102544,"end":1771181176370}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771181180531,"sessionID":"ses_39d61732dffeDSmzfjmxT906s1","part":{"id":"prt_c629ed3b5001KttsNSSRalqWbr","sessionID":"ses_39d61732dffeDSmzfjmxT906s1","messageID":"msg_c629e8d8c001d436NwO9YXsLEy","type":"tool","callID":"call_0b3b2cf37b274a4ea5c1ff7f","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore specs/ directory comprehensively","prompt":"Explore the specs/ directory thoroughly to understand all application specifications. \n- Read all spec files\n- Understand the feature requirements\n- Identify what functionality needs to be implemented\n- Note any dependencies between features\n\nUse \"very thorough\" level exploration. Return a detailed summary of all specifications found."},"output":"task_id: ses_39d612c3effeDcNPFsRNFCw5mB (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n# Comprehensive Specifications Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored all 12 specification files in the specs/ directory. Here's a detailed analysis of the Game of Life application:\n\n---\n\n## Executive Overview\n\nThis is a **gamified Conway's Game of Life** with:\n- Level-based progression system (default 10 levels)\n- Resource management (Flux) for strategic cell placement\n- Pattern-based scoring system rewarding movement and oscillation\n- Cinematic transitions between levels\n- Full audio/visual sonification\n- Expert settings for parameter tuning\n\n---\n\n## Core Systems Architecture\n\n### 1. Simulation Engine (`simulation-engine.md`)\n**Purpose**: Core cellular automaton computation\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Conway's rules: Born with 3 neighbors, Survives with 2-3 neighbors\n- Toroidal boundaries (edges wrap around)\n- Age-based cell tracking (0 = dead, >0 = alive with age in generations)\n- Double-buffer pattern for state updates\n- Optimized with React refs to avoid re-renders\n\n**Data Structures**:\n```typescript\nGridType = number[][]  // Age-based storage\nRuleSet = { born: [3], survive: [2,3] }\n```\n\n**Performance**: Precomputed neighbor offsets, direct grid access\n\n---\n\n### 2. Canvas Rendering (`canvas-rendering.md`)\n**Purpose**: High-performance visual display with neon aesthetics\n\n**Visual Theme**:\n- Background: `#0a0a0f` (very dark blue-black)\n- Grid lines: `#1a1a2e` (subtle, toggleable with 'G')\n- Age-based colors:\n  - Age 0: Cyan `#00ffff` with 15px glow\n  - Age 1-2: React Blue `#61dafb` with 8px glow\n  - Age 3-5: Magenta `#ff00ff` with 4px glow\n  - Age 6+: Deep Purple `#4a00ff` with 2px glow\n\n**Responsive Design**:\n- Mobile: 18px cells (min 10 visible)\n- Desktop: 20px cells\n- DPR scaling for sharp rendering\n\n**Visual Metric**: `--life-intensity` CSS variable (0-1 based on cell count)\n\n---\n\n### 3. Audio Sonification (`audio-sonification.md`)\n**Purpose**: Real-time sound generation from game events\n\n**Sound Types**:\n1. **Generation Sounds**: Triggered on cell births\n   - Pitch mapped to average row position (top = higher, bottom = lower)\n   - Intensity based on number of births\n   - Waveforms: sine, triangle, square, sawtooth\n   \n2. **Interaction Sounds**: Draw (high pitch ~880Hz), Erase (low pitch ~440Hz)\n\n**Audio Parameters**:\n- Volume: 0.0-0.5 (default 0.1)\n- Duration: 100-200ms (generation), 50ms (interaction)\n- Lazy initialization on first user gesture (browser requirement)\n\n---\n\n## Game Flow & State Management\n\n### 4. Phase Management (`phase-management.md`)\n**Purpose**: State machine governing game progression\n\n**Three Core Phases**:\n\n| Phase | Duration | Allowed Actions | Exit Condition |\n|-------|----------|-----------------|----------------|\n| **PLANNING** | Unlimited | Place/remove cells with Flux | Click START button |\n| **COUNTDOWN** | 3s | None (view only) | Countdown completes |\n| **RUNNING** | Level timer (45s base) | Place cells (add-only) | Timer = 0 OR all cells die |\n| **FINISHED** | 2.0s | None | Auto-advance to next level |\n\n**State Machine**:\n```typescript\nGamePhase = 'PLANNING' | 'COUNTDOWN' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED'\n```\n\n**Key Rules**:\n- START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n- No input allowed during countdown\n- Timer continues even when tab inactive\n- No simulation carryover between levels\n\n---\n\n### 5. Level Progression (`level-progression.md`)\n**Purpose**: Progressive difficulty system\n\n**Default Scaling** (Time Only mode):\n```\nLevel 1: 45s time, 20 Flux\nLevel 2: 60s time, 20 Flux\nLevel 3: 75s time, 20 Flux\n... each level adds 15s time\n```\n\n**Alternative Difficulty Modes** (expert settings):\n- **Time Only**: Increase time, constant Flux\n- **Resource Only**: Constant time, decrease Flux\n- **Mixed**: Both time and Flux adjusted\n- **Extreme**: Slight time increase, aggressive Flux reduction\n\n**Victory Condition**: Complete all levels (default 10), show total score\n\n**No Lose Condition**: Game always advances; only score accumulation varies\n\n---\n\n### 6. Auto-Advance Transitions (`auto-advance-transitions.md`)\n**Purpose**: Cinematic level transitions\n\n**Transition Sequence** (Success):\n1. **FINISHED Display** (2.0s): Show final score, \"Level Complete\", visual-only simulation\n2. **Fade Out** (2.0s): Black overlay opacity 0→1\n3. **Interstitial** (2.0s): Black screen, \"Level X Complete\" → \"Level X+1\", load next level, reset state\n4. **Fade In** (2.0s): Black overlay 1→0, new level visible, simulation stopped\n5. **READY**: Player can place cells\n\n**Skip Mechanism**: Press Space/ESC to skip to READY at any point\n\n**Edge Cases**:\n- Tab switches mid-transition: Pause timer, resume when active\n- Last level: Victory screen with total score\n- No simulation carryover between levels\n\n---\n\n## Gameplay Mechanics\n\n### 7. Flux Management (`flux-management.md`)\n**Purpose**: Strategic resource system\n\n**Core Rules**:\n- **Initial Flux**: 20 per level (configurable 5-50)\n- **Placement Cost**: 1 Flux per cell (both phases)\n- **Refunds**: Available during PLANNING phase (click to remove = +1 Flux)\n- **Play Phase**: Add-only (no removals)\n- **Strategic Choice**: Balance planning vs play-phase spending\n\n**UI Feedback**:\n- Green/Yellow: Plenty remaining\n- Orange: < 30% remaining\n- Red: 0 remaining (placement disabled)\n\n**State Structure**:\n```typescript\nFluxState {\n  current: number;     // Available\n  initial: number;     // Starting amount\n  placed: number;      // Total cells placed\n  removed: number;     // Total cells removed\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. Scoring System (`scoring-system.md`)\n**Purpose**: Real-time points based on pattern classification\n\n**Scoring Formula** (per generation):\n```typescript\nscore = (movers × 10 + oscillators × 2) × multiplier\n```\n\n**Pattern Rewards** (configurable):\n- **MOVER**: 10 points/generation (high reward for movement)\n- **OSCILLATOR**: 2 points/generation (small reward for activity)\n- **STATIC**: 0 points\n\n**Score Display**:\n- Top-left large number with \"PTS\" label\n- Smooth counting animation (lerp over 0.2s)\n- Optional breakdown: Active Movers, Active Oscillators, Current Rate\n\n**Persistence**:\n- Score resets to 0 each level\n- High scores saved to localStorage per level\n\n**End-of-Level Stats**: Final Score, Time Survived, Patterns Created\n\n---\n\n### 9. Movement Detection (`movement-detection.md`)\n**Purpose**: Classify cellular patterns by tracking centroids\n\n**Algorithm**:\n1. **Connected Component Detection**: Find clusters of adjacent cells (8-connectivity)\n2. **Centroid Tracking**: Track centroids over N generations (default: 5)\n3. **Classification**:\n   - **MOVER**: Centroid translates (>0.5 cell distance)\n   - **OSCILLATOR**: Centroid static but cell set changes\n   - **STATIC**: Centroid static, cell set unchanged\n\n**Data Structures**:\n```typescript\nTrackedCluster {\n  centroidHistory: {x,y}[]  // Last N positions\n  velocity: {dx, dy}        // Movement vector\n  classification: 'MOVER' | 'OSCILLATOR' | 'STATIC'\n}\n```\n\n**Performance Requirements**: Must process in <16ms for 60fps with 60×80 grids\n\n**Edge Cases**:\n- Cluster splits: Track both as new clusters\n- Cluster merges: Reset classification (avoid double-counting)\n- Glider guns: Gun is STATIC, produced gliders are MOVERS\n- Single cells: Minimum cluster size configurable (default 1)\n\n---\n\n## User Interaction Systems\n\n### 10. User Interaction (`user-interaction.md`)\n**Purpose**: Mouse/touch input handling for drawing\n\n**Interaction Modes**:\n- **Draw Mode**: Click/drag to place live cells (age=1)\n- **Erase Mode**: Click/drag to remove cells (set to 0)\n\n**Mouse Events**:\n- Down: Capture position, convert to grid coords, trigger interaction\n- Move (while pressed): Track cursor, trigger interaction\n- Up (global): Clear mouse down state\n- Leave canvas: Stop drag state\n\n**Touch Events**:\n- Prevent default (stop scrolling)\n- Single-touch only (ignore additional touches)\n- Touch-action: none on canvas\n\n**Coordinate Mapping**:\n```typescript\ncol = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))\nrow = floor(y / (canvasHeight / numRows))\n```\n\n**Dependencies**: Simulation engine (grid/dimensions), Audio (sounds), Canvas (redraws)\n\n---\n\n### 11. Grid Interaction (`grid-interaction.md`)\n**Purpose**: Direct cell manipulation during PLANNING phase\n\n**Core Mechanics**:\n- **Click to Place**: On empty cell, places live cell\n- **Click to Remove**: On live cell, removes and refunds Flux (PLANNING only)\n- **Minimum Cells Rule**: START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n\n**Cursor States**:\n- Default: Standard\n- Over empty (placeable): Crosshair\n- Over empty (unplaceable): Forbidden symbol (Flux=0)\n- Over live cell (removable): Minus icon\n\n**Visual Feedback**:\n- Cell preview ghost follows cursor\n- Placement: Fade-in (0.1s)\n- Removal: Shrink (0.15s)\n- Invalid action: Red flash\n\n**Constraints**:\n- Disabled during RUNNING and FINISHED phases\n- Touch targets: Minimum 44×44px (mobile accessibility)\n- Pinch-to-zoom disabled on grid\n\n---\n\n### 12. UI Overlay System (`ui-overlay.md`)\n**Purpose**: Controls, panels, and visual overlays\n\n**Components**:\n\n**A. Cinematic Intro Overlay**:\n- Title: \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch effect\n- CTA: \"ENTER VOID\" button\n- Exit: 1.2s fade/scale transition\n\n**B. Glass HUD Container** (floating overlay):\n- **Main Controls**: PLAY/PAUSE, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR\n- **Interaction Modes**: DRAW, ERASE buttons\n- **Status Controls**: Waveform selector (Sine/Triangle/Square/Saw), Volume slider (0-0.5), Generation counter, Settings toggle\n\n**C. Settings Panel**:\n- Speed slider (10ms-500ms)\n- Grid size: Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n- Visuals: Show grid lines checkbox\n- Audio: Enable sonification checkbox\n- Expert Settings access\n\n**D. Phase Status Display**:\n- Current phase indicator\n- Timer (COUNTDOWN, RUNNING)\n- Flux counter (PLANNING, RUNNING)\n\n**Styling**: Glass effect (blur, semi-transparent background, border)\n\n**Responsive**: Desktop (centered at bottom), Mobile (stacked/scrollable)\n\n---\n\n## Expert Settings (`expert-settings.md`)\n**Purpose**: Hidden configuration interface for tuning and debugging\n\n**Access Methods**:\n- Keyboard: Backtick (`) key\n- Menu: Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\n- Mobile: Triple-tap top-left corner\n\n**Configurable Parameters**:\n\n**Movement Detection**:\n- Centroid history length: 3-10 (default: 5)\n- Movement threshold: 0.1-2.0 (default: 0.5)\n- Min cluster size: 1-5 (default: 1)\n\n**Scoring**:\n- Mover points/gen: 1-100 (default: 10)\n- Oscillator points/gen: 0-20 (default: 2)\n- Score multiplier: 0.1-5.0 (default: 1.0)\n\n**Level Generation**:\n- Base time: 10-120s (default: 45s)\n- Time increment: 0-60s (default: 15s)\n- Base Flux: 5-50 (default: 20)\n- Difficulty mode: TIME_ONLY | RESOURCE_ONLY | MIXED | EXTREME\n\n**Grid Sizing**:\n- Mobile cell size: 14-24px (default: 18px)\n- Desktop cell size: 16-28px (default: 20px)\n\n**Features**:\n- Real-time updates (no restart required)\n- Persistence: localStorage under `gol-expert-settings`\n- Export/Import JSON for sharing configs\n- \"Reset to Defaults\" with confirmation\n- Optional presets: Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos\n\n---\n\n## Feature Dependencies\n\n**Critical Dependencies**:\n\n```\n[Simulation Engine]\n    ↓ provides grid state\n[Canvas Rendering] ← draws grid\n[User Interaction] ← modifies grid\n[Movement Detection] ← analyzes grid\n[Flux Management] ← limits placement\n    ↓\n[Scoring System] ← uses movement detection\n    ↓\n[Phase Management] ← controls game flow\n    ↓\n[Level Progression] ← manages levels\n    ↓\n[Auto-Advance Transitions] ← handles level changes\n\n[Audio Sonification]\n    ↖ from User Interaction (draw/erase sounds)\n    ↖ from Simulation Engine (generation sounds)\n\n[UI Overlay System]\n    ↖ controls all systems\n    ↖ shows phase status, flux, score\n\n[Expert Settings]\n    ↖ tunes parameters for all systems\n```\n\n**Dependency Details**:\n\n1. **Simulation Engine** is foundational - everything depends on grid state\n2. **User Interaction** requires:\n   - Simulation engine (grid dimensions)\n   - Audio system (interaction sounds)\n   - Canvas rendering (redraws on change)\n   \n3. **Movement Detection** requires:\n   - Simulation engine (grid state)\n   - Scoring system (to classify for points)\n   \n4. **Scoring System** requires:\n   - Movement detection (pattern classification)\n   - Expert settings (scoring parameters)\n   \n5. **Phase Management** requires:\n   - Flux management (can't start without cells)\n   - Simulation engine (stops/starts simulation)\n   \n6. **Level Progression** requires:\n   - Phase management (FINISHED triggers advance)\n   - Auto-advance transitions (fade effects)\n   \n7. **Auto-Advance Transitions** requires:\n   - Phase management (knows when FINISHED)\n   - Level progression (loads next level)\n   - Simulation engine (resets state)\n   \n8. **UI Overlay System** is the orchestrator:\n   - Controls simulation (PLAY/PAUSE)\n   - Shows phase status\n   - Displays flux and score\n   - Provides settings\n   - Toggles audio\n   \n9. **Audio Sonification** integrates with:\n   - User interaction (draw/erase sounds)\n   - Simulation engine (generation sounds)\n   - UI settings (volume, waveform, enable)\n\n10. **Expert Settings** tunes:\n    - Movement detection thresholds\n    - Scoring multipliers\n    - Level generation parameters\n    - Grid sizing\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Priority\n\n**Phase 1 - Core Foundation**:\n1. Simulation Engine (grid computation)\n2. Canvas Rendering (visual display)\n3. User Interaction (mouse/touch input)\n4. UI Overlay (basic controls)\n\n**Phase 2 - Game Mechanics**:\n5. Phase Management (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED)\n6. Flux Management (resource system)\n7. Movement Detection (pattern classification)\n8. Scoring System (points calculation)\n\n**Phase 3 - Game Flow**:\n9. Level Progression (difficulty scaling)\n10. Auto-Advance Transitions (cinematic fades)\n\n**Phase 4 - Polish & Advanced**:\n11. Audio Sonification (sound generation)\n12. Expert Settings (parameter tuning)\n\n---\n\n## Key Technical Constraints\n\n1. **Performance**: Movement detection must process 60×80 grids in <16ms (60fps)\n2. **Accessibility**: Touch targets minimum 44×44px on mobile\n3. **Browser**: AudioContext requires user gesture (autoplay policy)\n4. **Storage**: localStorage for expert settings and high scores\n5. **Responsive**: 18px cells mobile, 20px desktop\n6. **Timing**: Uses Date.now() or performance.now() for accurate timers\n7. **State Management**: Uses React refs for performance-critical data\n\n---\n\n## Edge Cases Summary\n\n| System | Key Edge Cases |\n|--------|---------------|\n| Simulation | Empty grid, static patterns, grid resizing, rapid speed changes |\n| Rendering | Canvas resize, high cell count (500+), empty grid |\n| Audio | No births, suspended context, volume=0, concurrent sounds |\n| Phase Management | Zero cells at start, early cell death, tab switch, rapid clicking |\n| Level Progression | Level 0/invalid, last level, browser refresh, all cells die early |\n| Transitions | Tab during transition, rapid success, last level, interruption |\n| Flux | Zero flux start, accidental removal, play-phase placement timing |\n| Scoring | Score overflow, negative multiplier, zero points generation |\n| Movement Detection | Cluster split/merge, oscillator periods, glider guns, single cells |\n| User Interaction | Boundary coordinates, rapid clicking, canvas resize, touch conflicts |\n| Grid Interaction | Rapid clicking, edge of grid, overlapping with UI, window resize |\n| UI Overlay | Intro exit timing, UI hidden state, settings during run, grid size change |\n| Expert Settings | Invalid values, changes while running, reset during game, corrupted storage |\n\n---\n\nThis application is a sophisticated gamification of Conway's Game of Life with comprehensive resource management, pattern recognition, and progression systems. All 12 spec files are well-integrated with clear dependencies and a cohesive design vision.\n</task_result>","title":"Explore specs/ directory comprehensively","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d612c3effeDcNPFsRNFCw5mB","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771181102014,"end":1771181180528}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771181251930,"sessionID":"ses_39d61732dffeDSmzfjmxT906s1","part":{"id":"prt_c629ed5be001dMV3owfY9qeOdv","sessionID":"ses_39d61732dffeDSmzfjmxT906s1","messageID":"msg_c629e8d8c001d436NwO9YXsLEy","type":"tool","callID":"call_436ed597289542cc9eaf6645","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore src/ directory structure and code","prompt":"Explore the src/ directory comprehensively to understand the current implementation:\n- Map out the directory structure\n- Identify all source files and their purposes\n- Understand the current state of implementation\n- Note what functionality exists vs what might be missing\n- Identify key components and their relationships\n\nUse \"very thorough\" level exploration. Return a detailed summary of the codebase structure and current implementation state."},"output":"task_id: ses_39d612a3affecmLHt2r5CPPInA (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n# Comprehensive Codebase Exploration: Game of Life\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThis is **Conway's Game of Life** implemented as a strategic cellular automaton puzzle game using **React 19.2.4 + TypeScript 5.9.3 + Vite 7.3.1**. The project demonstrates excellent architecture with clear separation of concerns, comprehensive type definitions, and extensive test coverage (22 source files, 16 test files, ~4,892 lines of TypeScript code).\n\n---\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── components/          # React UI components (7 files)\n├── lib/                 # Core business logic (11 files)\n├── hooks/               # Custom React hooks (1 file)\n├── styles/              # CSS stylesheets (4 files)\n├── types/               # TypeScript type definitions (1 file)\n├── test/                # Test configuration (1 file)\n├── App.tsx              # Root application component\n├── main.tsx             # Entry point\n└── [16 test files]      # Comprehensive test suite\n```\n\n---\n\n## Technology Stack\n\n| Technology | Version | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|---------|\n| React | 19.2.4 | UI Framework |\n| TypeScript | 5.9.3 | Type-safe development (strict mode) |\n| Vite | 7.3.1 | Build tool & dev server |\n| Vitest | 4.0.18 | Testing framework |\n| Testing Library | 16.3.2 | Component testing |\n| ESLint + Prettier | Latest | Code quality |\n\n---\n\n## Core Components Analysis\n\n### 1. **Simulation Engine** (`src/lib/simulation.ts`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Features**:\n- Conway's Game of Life rules (born: [3], survive: [2,3])\n- Toroidal boundary handling (wrap-around edges)\n- Age-based cell tracking (0=dead, >0=alive with age)\n- Grid operations: create, clear, random fill\n- Neighbor counting with precomputed offsets\n- Three grid presets: Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n\n**Key Functions**:\n```typescript\ncreateGrid(rows, cols) → GridType\napplyRules(grid, rules) → StepResult\nstepSimulation(state) → SimulationResult\ncountNeighbors(grid, row, col) → number\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Game Phase Management** (`src/lib/phase.ts`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Phases**: PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED\n\n**Features**:\n- State machine with valid transitions\n- Countdown timer (3 seconds)\n- Running timer (configurable duration, default 45s)\n- Phase blockers (e.g., \"Need at least 1 cell to start\")\n- Visibility change handling (pause/resume when tab hidden)\n\n**Implementation**: Reducer pattern with PhaseAction types\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Flux Management System** (`src/lib/flux.ts`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Purpose**: Resource management for placing cells\n\n**Features**:\n- Track current/initial flux, cells placed/removed\n- Can place cell if flux >= 1\n- Refund cell only during PLANNING phase\n- Color-coded display (green/yellow/orange/red based on ratio)\n\n**State Structure**:\n```typescript\ninterface FluxState {\n  current: number;      // Available flux\n  initial: number;      // Starting flux (20 default)\n  placed: number;       // Cells placed\n  removed: number;      // Cells removed (refunded)\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Movement Detection & Pattern Tracking** (`src/lib/movement.ts`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Features**:\n- Connected components detection (BFS, 8-connectivity)\n- Cluster matching across generations (centroid-based)\n- Velocity calculation from centroid history\n- Pattern classification: MOVER, OSCILLATOR, STATIC\n\n**Key Functions**:\n```typescript\nfindConnectedComponents(grid, generation) → CellCluster[]\nmatchClusters(current, previous) → Map<string, TrackedCluster>\ntrackClusters(current, previous, config) → TrackedCluster[]\ncalculateVelocity(history) → {dx, dy}\n```\n\n**Classification Logic**:\n- **MOVER**: Velocity > threshold\n- **OSCILLATOR**: Static centroid but cells change\n- **STATIC**: No movement, no cell changes\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Scoring System** (`src/lib/scoring.ts`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Features**:\n- Points per generation based on pattern classification\n- Configurable scoring (movers: 10pts, oscillators: 2pts)\n- Score multiplier support\n- Milestone detection (every 100 points)\n- Animated score display with pulse effects\n\n**Configuration**:\n```typescript\ninterface ScoringConfig {\n  moverPointsPerGeneration: 10;\n  oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: 2;\n  scoreMultiplier: 1.0;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Canvas Rendering** (`src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Features**:\n- High-DPI canvas support (devicePixelRatio)\n- Age-based cell coloring (5 color presets)\n- Glow effects with blur\n- Grid line toggle\n- Responsive cell size (18px mobile, 20px desktop)\n- Performance optimized (draw callback memoization)\n\n**Color Scheme**:\n- Age 0: #00ffff (cyan)\n- Age 1-2: #61dafb (light blue)\n- Age 3-5: #ff00ff (magenta)\n- Age 6+: #4a00ff (purple)\n\n---\n\n### 7. **User Interaction** (`src/components/GridInteraction.tsx`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Features**:\n- Mouse and touch support\n- Draw/Erase modes\n- Flux-aware placement (cannot place if flux=0)\n- Phase-locked interaction (only PLANNING phase)\n- Hover cursor feedback (crosshair/placeable, not-allowed/locked)\n- Cell highlighting on hover (color-coded by action)\n\n**Interaction Flow**:\n1. User clicks/taps canvas\n2. Convert to grid coordinates\n3. Check phase and flux\n4. Update grid and flux state\n5. Trigger re-render\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Glass HUD** (`src/components/GlassHUD.tsx`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Features**:\n- Glassmorphism design (blur, transparency)\n- Control groups: Simulation, Mode, Grid Size, View\n- Status display: Phase, Timer, Generation, Cells, Flux\n- Responsive layout (mobile-friendly)\n- Disabled state handling during non-PLANNING phases\n\n**Controls**:\n- STEP (manual advance)\n- START/RUNNING (auto-play)\n- RANDOM (random fill)\n- CLEAR (reset)\n- DRAW/ERASE toggle\n- Small/Medium/Large grid presets\n- Show/Hide grid lines\n- Settings button (⚙️)\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Score Display** (`src/components/ScoreDisplay.tsx`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Features**:\n- Animated score counter (200ms ease-out transition)\n- Pulse effect on score change\n- Milestone flash animation (color cycle)\n- Formatted display (e.g., \"1.2M\", \"15.5K\")\n- Pattern breakdown option (movers, oscillators, rate)\n\n---\n\n### 10. **Phase Timer Hook** (`src/hooks/usePhaseTimer.ts`)\n**Status**: ✅ **Fully Implemented**\n\n**Features**:\n- Handles countdown and running timers\n- Visibility change detection (pause when tab hidden)\n- Automatic phase transitions\n- Timer cleanup on unmount\n- Ref-based interval management\n\n---\n\n## Type System (`src/types/index.ts`)\n\n**Status**: ✅ **Comprehensive (110 lines)**\n\n**Key Types**:\n- GridType, GamePhase, InteractionMode, TransitionState\n- CellCluster, TrackedCluster\n- RuleSet, SimulationState, FluxState\n- LevelConfig, ScoringConfig, ScoreState\n- LevelProgression, DifficultyScalingMode\n- TransitionConfig, MovementDetectionParams\n- GridSizingParams, AudioParams, ExpertSettings\n\n---\n\n## Component Relationships\n\n```\nApp (root)\n └─ Game (main container)\n     ├─ ScoreDisplay (top-left, fixed)\n     ├─ GlassHUD (bottom-center, fixed)\n     └─ GridInteraction\n         └─ CanvasGrid\n```\n\n**Data Flow**:\n1. **Game** maintains all state (grid, flux, phase, score, generation)\n2. **usePhaseTimer** manages phase transitions and timers\n3. **GridInteraction** handles user input, updates grid/flux\n4. **CanvasGrid** renders the grid\n5. **GlassHUD** displays controls and status\n6. **ScoreDisplay** shows animated score\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Status\n\n### ✅ **Fully Implemented** (110/175 items, ~63%)\n\n**Core Systems**:\n- ✅ Project setup & build system\n- ✅ Type definitions\n- ✅ Shared utilities (validation, logger, state management)\n- ✅ Simulation engine (Conway's rules, toroidal boundaries)\n- ✅ Phase management (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED)\n- ✅ Flux management (resource system)\n- ✅ Movement detection (connected components, tracking)\n- ✅ Scoring system (points, milestones)\n- ✅ Canvas rendering (high-DPI, age-based colors)\n- ✅ Grid interaction (mouse/touch, draw/erase)\n- ✅ Glass HUD (controls, status display)\n- ✅ Score display (animated, formatted)\n- ✅ Phase timer hook (visibility handling)\n- ✅ Intro overlay (glitch effect)\n- ✅ UI toggle button\n\n### ❌ **Not Implemented** (65/175 items, ~37%)\n\n**Missing Features**:\n\n1. **Advanced Visual Effects**:\n   - Cell birth/death animations\n   - Movement animations\n   - Pattern highlighting\n\n2. **Settings Panel** (`src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`):\n   - Speed control\n   - Grid size controls (in addition to presets)\n   - Visual controls (cell size, colors)\n   - Audio controls (waveform, volume)\n   - Expert settings access\n\n3. **Level Progression** (`src/lib/level.ts`):\n   - Level configuration system\n   - Progression state management\n   - Level display UI\n   - End-of-game handling\n\n4. **Transitions System** (`src/lib/transitions.ts`):\n   - Fade out/in animations\n   - Interstitial screens\n   - Auto-advance with skip\n   - Transition audio\n\n5. **Victory Screen** (`src/components/VictoryScreen.tsx`):\n   - End-of-level stats\n   - Pattern breakdown\n   - High score persistence\n\n6. **Audio Sonification** (`src/lib/audio.ts`):\n   - Sound engine\n   - Waveform-based audio\n   - Volume control\n\n---\n\n## Test Coverage\n\n**Total Test Files**: 16\n- **Library Tests**: 9 files (flux, interaction, logger, movement, phase, scoring, simulation, state, validation)\n- **Component Tests**: 7 files (CanvasGrid, GlassHUD, GridInteraction, IntroOverlay, ScoreDisplay, UIToggleButton, App)\n\n**Test Setup**:\n- Vitest with jsdom environment\n- localStorage mock\n- @testing-library/react for component testing\n- Global test setup in `src/test/setup.ts`\n\n**Coverage Highlights**:\n- All core library functions tested\n- Component rendering and interaction tested\n- Edge cases and boundary conditions covered\n- Async behavior tested (timers, animations)\n\n---\n\n## Code Quality Assessment\n\n### ✅ **Strengths**:\n\n1. **Clean Architecture**: Clear separation between UI components and business logic\n2. **Type Safety**: Comprehensive TypeScript types with strict mode\n3. **Modularity**: Well-organized library functions, pure functions preferred\n4. **Testing**: Extensive test coverage for core functionality\n5. **Performance**: Optimizations include ref usage, memoized callbacks, requestAnimationFrame\n6. **Code Style**: Consistent formatting with Prettier, ESLint configured\n7. **Documentation**: Type definitions serve as inline documentation\n8. **Responsive Design**: Mobile-friendly layouts and touch support\n9. **Accessibility**: ARIA labels, keyboard support considered\n10. **Error Handling**: Validation, boundary checks, try-catch blocks\n\n### 🔶 **Areas for Improvement**:\n\n1. **Missing Features**: 37% of planned features not implemented\n2. **Settings Integration**: Settings button exists but panel not implemented\n3. **Persistence**: No localStorage integration for game state (only mocked in tests)\n4. **Accessibility**: Could be enhanced (focus management, screen reader support)\n5. **Performance**: Large grids (60×80) may need optimization (WebGL, Web Workers)\n6. **Internationalization**: No i18n support\n7. **Analytics**: No telemetry or usage tracking\n\n---\n\n## Key Technical Decisions\n\n1. **React + Vite**: Chosen for performance and developer experience\n2. **Canvas API**: Used for grid rendering (better performance than DOM for large grids)\n3. **Age-based Cell Storage**: Integer values track cell age for visual effects\n4. **Toroidal Boundaries**: Wrap-around edges for continuous simulation\n5. **Reducer Pattern**: Used for phase management and complex state\n6. **Double Buffering**: New grid created each generation to avoid mutation\n7. **Connected Components**: BFS for detecting cell clusters\n8. **Centroid Tracking**: Pattern matching using cluster centroids across generations\n9. **Flux System**: Resource management adds strategic depth\n10. **Phase Machine**: Structured game flow with clear states\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n**Production**:\n- react, react-dom (minimal dependencies)\n\n**Development**:\n- vite, @vitejs/plugin-react (build tooling)\n- typescript (type safety)\n- vitest, @testing-library/react (testing)\n- eslint, prettier (code quality)\n\n---\n\n## Build & Development Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `npm run dev` | Start development server |\n| `npm run build` | Build for production |\n| `npm run preview` | Preview production build |\n| `npm run lint` | Run ESLint |\n| `npm run typecheck` | Run TypeScript type checking |\n| `npm run format` | Format code with Prettier |\n| `npm run test` | Run tests in watch mode |\n| `npm run test:run` | Run tests once |\n| `npm run test:ui` | Run tests with UI |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Patterns\n\n1. **Component-Based**: React functional components with hooks\n2. **Container/Presentational**: Game component as container, others as presentational\n3. **Custom Hooks**: usePhaseTimer for reusable logic\n4. **Pure Functions**: Library functions are pure and testable\n5. **Reducer Pattern**: Phase and state management\n6. **Observer Pattern**: React's subscription model for state updates\n7. **Strategy Pattern**: Configurable rule sets, scoring configs\n8. **Factory Pattern**: Action creators, state creators\n\n---\n\n## Design System\n\n### Colors:\n- Primary: #61dafb (light blue)\n- Accent: #00ffff (cyan), #ff00ff (magenta)\n- Background: #0a0a0f (dark)\n- Text: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.87)\n\n### Effects:\n- Glassmorphism: backdrop-filter: blur(10px)\n- Glow: box-shadow with color\n- Blur: cell age-based glow blur\n- Pulse: CSS animations\n\n### Typography:\n- Font: Inter, system-ui\n- Monospace: Courier New for numbers\n- Sizing: Responsive (0.8rem - 3rem)\n\n---\n\n## Future Potential\n\nThe codebase provides a solid foundation for:\n1. **Multiplayer**: WebSocket integration for collaborative play\n2. **AI Patterns**: Machine learning to predict optimal moves\n3. **Custom Rules**: User-defined rule sets beyond Conway\n4. **VR/AR**: Three.js integration for 3D visualization\n5. **Game Modes**: Puzzle mode, time attack, sandbox\n6. **Social Features**: Leaderboards, pattern sharing\n7. **Analytics**: Pattern detection, statistics\n8. **Modding**: Plugin system for extensions\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThis is a **well-architected, production-ready foundation** for a Game of Life puzzle game. The core mechanics are **fully functional** with **excellent code quality**, **comprehensive testing**, and **modern development practices**. \n\n**Key Achievement**: 110/175 implementation items completed (63%), with all critical systems operational.\n\n**Immediate Priorities** (based on implementation plan):\n1. Implement Settings Panel for expert configuration\n2. Add Level Progression system\n3. Implement audio sonification\n4. Add transition animations and interstitial screens\n5. Enhance with cell birth/death animations\n\nThe codebase demonstrates **professional React/TypeScript development** with **clean architecture**, **strong typing**, and **thoughtful design**. It's ready for incremental feature development and could serve as an excellent foundation for a full-featured game.\n</task_result>","title":"Explore src/ directory structure and code","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d612a3affecmLHt2r5CPPInA","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771181102530,"end":1771181251927}}}}
