{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771181403533,"sessionID":"ses_39d61732dffeDSmzfjmxT906s1","part":{"id":"prt_c62a36d860018yss0ZrQaqXHPN","sessionID":"ses_39d61732dffeDSmzfjmxT906s1","messageID":"msg_c62a35c9a001I3BFfWpI1VFe0D","type":"tool","callID":"call_ad8ab7c1792d497eaa159ea9","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/audio-sonification.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/audio-sonification.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Audio Sonification System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The audio sonification system generates real-time sounds based on simulation birth events and user interactions using the Web Audio API, providing audio feedback for cellular automaton behavior.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Sound Engine Interface\n9: \n10: ```typescript\n11: interface SoundEngine {\n12:   setEnabled(enabled: boolean): void;\n13:   setVolume(volume: number): void;\n14:   setWaveform(waveform: OscillatorType): void;\n15:   playGenerationSound(bornCount: number, avgRow: number, totalRows: number): void;\n16:   playInteractionSound(type: 'draw' | 'erase'): void;\n17: }\n18: ```\n19: \n20: ### Generation Sounds\n21: \n22: **Trigger**: After each simulation step with bornCount > 0\n23: \n24: **Pitch Mapping**:\n25: - Based on average row position of new births\n26: - Formula: `pitch = (1 - avgRow / totalRows) * frequencyRange`\n27: - Higher rows (top) = higher pitch\n28: - Lower rows (bottom) = lower pitch\n29: \n30: **Intensity Mapping**:\n31: - Based on number of births: bornCount\n32: - More births = louder/more prominent sound\n33: \n34: **Waveform Types**:\n35: - `sine`: Smooth, pure tone (default)\n36: - `triangle`: Slightly richer harmonics\n37: - `square`: Harsh, buzzy tone\n38: - `sawtooth`: Bright, brassy tone\n39: \n40: ### Interaction Sounds\n41: \n42: **Draw Sound**:\n43: - Triggered when placing a cell\n44: - Higher pitch, short duration\n45: \n46: **Erase Sound**:\n47: - Triggered when removing a cell\n48: - Lower pitch, short duration\n49: \n50: ### Volume Control\n51: \n52: - **Range**: 0.0 to 0.5\n53: - **Default**: 0.1 (10%)\n54: - **UI Slider**: 10ms steps, displays percentage (volume * 200%)\n55: \n56: ## Implementation Architecture\n57: \n58: ### Audio Context\n59: \n60: ```typescript\n61: class SoundEngine {\n62:   private audioContext: AudioContext | null = null;\n63:   private enabled: boolean = true;\n64:   private volume: number = 0.1;\n65:   private waveform: OscillatorType = 'sine';\n66: \n67:   // ... methods\n68: }\n69: ```\n70: \n71: ### Sound Generation Process\n72: \n73: 1. **Initialize Context**: Create on first user interaction (browser requirement)\n74: 2. **Create Oscillator**: Generate sound with configured waveform\n75: 3. **Create Gain Node**: Control volume and envelope\n76: 4. **Connect Nodes**: Oscillator → Gain → Destination\n77: 5. **Set Parameters**: Frequency based on data, volume from setting\n78: 6. **Envelope**: Quick attack, exponential decay\n79: 7. **Cleanup**: Stop and disconnect after sound completes\n80: \n81: ### Lazy Initialization\n82: \n83: - AudioContext created on first sound play\n84: - Handles browser autoplay policies\n85: - Resumes context if suspended\n86: \n87: ## Audio Parameters\n88: \n89: ### Generation Sound\n90: ```typescript\n91: interface GenerationSoundParams {\n92:   frequency: number;    // Derived from row position\n93:   duration: number;     // Short, ~100-200ms\n94:   volume: number;       // baseVolume * bornCount scaling\n95:   waveform: OscillatorType;\n96: }\n97: ```\n98: \n99: ### Interaction Sound\n100: ```typescript\n101: interface InteractionSoundParams {\n102:   drawFrequency: number;    // Higher pitch (~880Hz)\n103:   eraseFrequency: number;   // Lower pitch (~440Hz)\n104:   duration: number;         // Very short (~50ms)\n105:   volume: number;          // baseVolume\n106:   waveform: OscillatorType;\n107: }\n108: ```\n109: \n110: ## Edge Cases\n111: \n112: 1. **No Births**: Sound not triggered\n113: 2. **Suspended Context**: Resume on next interaction\n114: 3. **Volume = 0**: Sounds generated but at 0 gain\n115: 4. **Disabled**: Engine returns early without generating sounds\n116: 5. **Multiple Events**: Concurrent sounds allowed (polyphonic)\n117: \n118: ## Browser Compatibility\n119: \n120: - Requires Web Audio API support\n121: - Modern browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\n122: - iOS: Requires user gesture to start\n123: - Autoplay policy: Context starts suspended\n124: \n125: ## Dependencies\n126: \n127: - Core simulation engine: Provides birth statistics\n128: - User interaction system: Triggers draw/erase sounds\n129: - UI/overlay system: Volume, waveform, enabled settings\n130: \n\n(End of file - total 130 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/audio-sonification.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Audio Sonification System\n\n## Overview\nThe audio sonification system generates real-time sounds based on simulation birth events and user interactions using the Web Audio API, providing audio feedback for cellular automaton behavior.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Sound Engine Interface\n\n```typescript\ninterface SoundEngine {\n  setEnabled(enabled: boolean): void;\n  setVolume(volume: number): void;\n  setWaveform(waveform: OscillatorType): void;\n  playGenerationSound(bornCount: number, avgRow: number, totalRows: number): void;\n  playInteractionSound(type: 'draw' | 'erase'): void;\n}\n```\n\n### Generation Sounds","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771181403527,"end":1771181403531}}}}
